      "reasoning": "All five earlier selections agree with the current choices and their own captured worked solutions. q-130523: multiplying the matrix by the variable column gives 10x+25y=15 and 12x+3y=-6; dividing these equations by 5 and 3 gives option 2. q-130528: the matrix rows give 5y=9 and x=-1, option 2. q-73531: I contains the discontinuity at x=1, II is not closed, and III is closed, bounded, and within the continuous domain; therefore III only. Its worked solution mistakenly names [-1,1] while discussing [-2,2], but this typo does not change the answer. q-12284: the coefficient matrix has determinant -1 and inverse [[1,-2],[2,-5]], giving the solution column (-7,-19), option 4. q-32136: the determinant is 5 and the inverse is (1/5)[[3,1],[-2,1]], giving (-3/5,2/5), option 3. In the last two choices, x denotes the full solution column rather than just its first component.",
